  "body": "Read optional parametric feature metadata from `document.json` inside SolidCraft `.sc` and `.solidcraft` containers to provide advisory hole and pocket hints in CamCraft.\n\n## Scope\n- Extend `crates/kernel/src/solidcraft/` and `crates/geometry/src/solidcraft.rs` to parse optional feature labels and hole or pocket parameters from `document.json` using only SolidCraft's published Apache-2.0 container schema.\n- Match parsed hints geometrically against CamCraft's recognized B-rep/mesh features (holes, bosses, pockets, slots, planar faces) without modifying mesh or toolpath geometry.\n- Surface matched labels as read-only advisory fields in `list_features`, `detect_holes`, or `detect_pockets`.\n- Enforce the Prime Directive: never trust CAD metadata over actual solid geometry. Missing, unknown, or corrupt metadata entries must degrade cleanly without failing the import.\n\nDone means: Tests on a `.sc` fixture confirm advisory feature labels appear beside geometrically recognized features, corrupt or absent feature metadata degrades cleanly without error, and geometric dimensions always override mismatched metadata.\n\nPart of #3793\n",
